[Music]  what's very important I feel is that you  make a design very site-specific so in  other words there is not much  justification for putting a building in  a certain place that could be anywhere  else in the world  so what we developed is essentially a  structure that could get very dense in  areas where you want to keep certain  environmental impacts out like the Sun  for example or you want to keep the rain  out and it could open up in other areas  like over here where you want to get  prevailing wind into the interior of the  space so this is a very finely tuned  structure that can react even to let's  say a tree that is sitting next to the  structure so where a tree would provide  shade there's no need for the structure  to get dense so it can open up so we did  projects where we looked at a very fine  kind of tuning in terms of environmental  factors of a facade of a rectangular  building so it can play out in a small  scale or on a big scale but the  underlying power of the parametric model  is that it can adapt very easily if you  change the parameters so it's not that  every time you change something in the  design you have to redraw it but let's  say you know you turn the building a  little bit everything would adjust  automatically  I have absolutely no doubt that these  technologies will be more and more  important in the future and in a way a  project like this is a great case to  make for a new way of designing  buildings  [Music]

